  "notes": [
    "DRAFT: a skeleton from the world database export of map 90 (tools/dungeongen, spec tools/dungeongen/plans.json). The boss order is the usual clear order, the packs are the spawn clusters nearest each boss; walls, doors, stairs and events are unknown to it. Not mapped, not live-checked: do the GM-invisible mapping walk and correct the route before the first run (AUTO-IMPROVE step 0); dungeon_run refuses it without allow_draft.",
    "The cave chain (moved from leg 0 to leg 1 by the route order fix: the 6223 Leprous Defender and 6233 Mechanized Sentry camps at x -517..-427, y 226..273, z -211.5..-207.8) is pulled from its east end westwards, one camp per step, radius 8, with an approach point on each camp's own floor 18-23 yd from it (first live run r20-19z39 slot 4: the tank pulled from the Holdout landing 21-36 yd above the packs and the ranged party stayed 60-70 yd behind while the whole cave joined the step). The two same-camp pairs (6223/6233 at 10.1 yd and the two 6233 rows at 6.7 yd) are one group each. Route into the cave: from the Holdout landing the navmesh goes (-548 147) (-530 115) east and up to (-448 240); it passes the 6220 at -445 174 within 1-8 yd; that pack is leg 1 pull group 4, ahead of the chain, so the chain's first pull only comes after it. The 6220 at -477 165 is not walked.",
    "The event NPCs 7897 (Alarm-a-bomb 2600, spawn 30134 at -573.6 126.1 -202.1) and 7849 (Mobile Alert System, spawns 30141 at -759.1 399.5 -272.6, 30144 at -804.3 531.5 -297.4 and 30143 at -738.3 655.9 -321.8) cannot be attacked by the party, so they are never pulled: the draft's pull groups that held them are gone (the 6329 pack at -582 137 -202 that held 7897's walk, the 6226 packs at -788 420 -273 and -798 538 -296, and the 6212 pack at -727 652 -309 beside the 7849 spawns), and every leg whose pull radius or route reaches a spawn skips it (leg 0 skips 7897; legs 2 and 3 skip 7849). First live run r21-19z40e slot 4: step 180 (leg 0) paused four times on 'a fight lasted more than 180 s' with 'entry 7897 ... is not on the tank yet; the party is held back' and 'attack ... refused: invalid-target: The group cannot attack that target'. The 7897's patrol corridor (x -573..-557, y 74..126, bomb at -561 110) lies 15-23 yd west of the tunnel walk's packs (-548 138 and -534 121): an approach hop that stopped inside it failed three times (r23 slot 4, 2026-10-23, at -566.8 78.8), so keep stands and approach hops out of it.",
    "A wait_for on a door a lever or key opens needs timeout_s 60 (the default): a linked door can open 30 s after the use.",
    "Needs: the gnome-face doors and their six buttons (GO_GNOME_FACE_1-6, GO_BUTTON_1-6) and the bomb faces before Thermaplugg",
    "Needs: Explosive Charges (GO_EXPLOSIVE_CHARGE) to open the north and south cave-ins (GO_CAVE_IN_NORTH/SOUTH) on the way in",
    "Needs: Grubbis (7361) has no spawn row",
    "The Back Entrance (trigger 523) puts the party deep inside; this plan starts at the front.",
    "Leg 3's lower-deck pack (leg 3 pull group 13, the 6212/6232 trio at -738.7 659.8 -323.4 r14.7) is a planned pull again, before the route to the old step 152 (-734.65 709.46 -317.98): the 2026-11-13 proof run (dr-proof-gnomer, slot 4) fought beside it for steps 152-154 and lost the tank first in all five fights there, and the same pack was a pull group of the deployed route (20261104160000 rows, pull group 15). Its entries, positions and radius are that old plan's (git show origin/dev:dungeons/gnomeregan.json, leg 3 pull group 15). The stand -732 671 -329 is the old plan's own lower-deck approach row ('pull group 18 approach'), 14.2 yd from the pack on the pack's floor; the navmesh walk down to it from step 151's point is 249.8 yd and the way back up to the step-152 pack 209.4 yd, so the plan check's detour warning for this group is the walk, as it was for the same group of the old plan."
  ],
